    "agent_last_message": "The tool is built and working. `cmake -B build && cmake --build build` run from `output/` compiles it with no warnings and produces `build/wordcount`.\n\nYour prompt doesn't name the executable, so I used `wordcount`, from the spec's title. If something expects a different name, change the `add_executable` line in `output/CMakeLists.txt`.\n\n```\nbuild/wordcount --input <file> --output <file>\n```\n\n## Decisions where the spec was silent\n\n- **Byte-oriented reading.** A character is a byte, and whitespace is exactly the six characters the spec lists. Lowercasing maps ASCII `A`\u2013`Z` only, so `\u00c9` and `\u00e9` stay different words. This keeps results identical on every machine.\n- **No file is \"malformed\" by content.** The spec defines every byte as a character, so any byte sequence is valid input. The JSON stays valid UTF-8 anyway: invalid sequences such as a Latin-1 `\u00e9` print as U+FFFD, and control characters are escaped. The counts still use the real bytes.\n- **Exit 1 for output problems.** An output path that can't be opened exits 1, as does `--input` and `--output` naming the same file. A write that fails after opening (disk full) exits 2. Bad input never creates or touches the output file.\n- **Strict arguments.** Repeated flags exit 1, and `--help` counts as unknown, since the spec names only two flags. `--input=path` is also accepted.\n\n## How I checked it\n\n- **Edge cases:** all of the spec's edge cases produce the stated values.\n- **Independent oracle:** about 27,000 random inputs, plus 100 MB files, match a separate Python implementation written from the spec. That includes inputs straddling the 256 KiB read boundary.\n- **Tests:** a unit suite (about 1.1M checks) and an end-to-end script run against the real binary. They also ran clean under AddressSanitizer and UBSan, with GCC 13 and 14, in Release and Debug. Deliberately injected bugs were caught.\n- **Counter size:** counters stay exact past 2\u00b3\u00b2 (4.5 billion words and 9 GB tested).\n- **Exit 2 paths:** exit 2 was confirmed f",
